* so vaddr and bias stuff is currently borked when pointer encoding
  (e.g. for LSDA) is absolute (e.g. u4 without pcrel). Keep testing
  with pic/pie for now.

* _start seems to be always wrong. Bad unwind info. Report upstream?
  The issue is us or at least some of it, we should more correctly
  flag/report unexpected entry state and then trust FDE data.

* replace <Various>::ToString() with AbslStringify

* IsFileBackedNonExecutable logic for table jumps might be a bit too
  pessimistic. I think I've seen binaries that for various reasons
  combined entire exec+read-only-data into big PT_LOAD segment
  (possibly huge-page aligned).

* ensure that we flag any cases where "CFG structure" is un-discovered
  (e.g. earlier bound is bottomed later). All cases like this need to
  be loudly REVIEWed or MISMATCHed.
